note over P, C
  Each child requires fresh terminal approval
  before work begins on its stated scope.
  Acquisition consent covers host downloads,
  not guest network access or any subsequent
  provider calls.
end note
note over C, STATE
  Write stage intent before provider calls
  so ambiguous failures leave a bound
  attempt for review.
  Keep that state for reconciliation rather
  than automatic retry, reset or removal.
end note
note over C, VM
  Policy acceptance binds one attempt, name
  and digest before copying starts.
  It records consent, not proof that deny
  rules prevail over broader allows or grant
  reusable F9 authority.
end note
note over P, VM
  Accept diagnostic completion only for the
  matching STOP report, not F9 qualification.
  A host CLI timeout proves neither guest
  termination nor permission to start Cargo,
  KUnit or model work.
end note

